{"content":[{"c":["REMISSION OF SINS*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["KJV phrase synonymous with “forgiveness of sins.” The NT uses a variety of terms to describe a single truth. With the concept of forgiveness of sins, there are a number of expressions employed (“passing over,” ",{"href":"?bref=Rom.3.25","r":"Rom.3.25","rawR":"Rom.3.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rom.3.25","value":"Rom.3.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"Rom 3:25"},"; “covered,” ",{"href":"?bref=Rom.4.7","r":"Rom.4.7","rawR":"Rom.4.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rom.4.7","value":"Rom.4.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Rom 4:7"},"; “not imputed,” ",{"href":"?bref=Rom.4.8","r":"Rom.4.8","rawR":"Rom.4.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rom.4.8","value":"Rom.4.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Rom 4:8"},"; “remembered no more,” ",{"href":"?bref=Heb.10.17","r":"Heb.10.17","rawR":"Heb.10.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Heb.10.17","value":"Heb.10.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Heb 10:17"},"). One of the most significant is the word rendered “remission” (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.26.28","r":"Matt.26.28","rawR":"Matt.26.28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.26.28","value":"Matt.26.28"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 26:28"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.1.4","r":"Mark.1.4","rawR":"Mark.1.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.1.4","value":"Mark.1.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mk 1:4"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.1.77","r":"Luke.1.77","rawR":"Luke.1.77","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.1.77","value":"Luke.1.77"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 1:77"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.3.3","r":"Luke.3.3","rawR":"Luke.3.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.3.3","value":"Luke.3.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"3:3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.24.47","r":"Luke.24.47","rawR":"Luke.24.47","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.24.47","value":"Luke.24.47"}],"t":"ref","v":"24:47"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Acts.2.38","r":"Acts.2.38","rawR":"Acts.2.38","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.2.38","value":"Acts.2.38"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 2:38"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Acts.10.43","r":"Acts.10.43","rawR":"Acts.10.43","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.10.43","value":"Acts.10.43"}],"t":"ref","v":"10:43"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Heb.9.22","r":"Heb.9.22","rawR":"Heb.9.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Heb.9.22","value":"Heb.9.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Heb 9:22"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Heb.10.18","r":"Heb.10.18","rawR":"Heb.10.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Heb.10.18","value":"Heb.10.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"10:18"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["The word has an interesting tradition in the Greek language. In the legal sense, it was used to denote dismissal from office, release from obligation, remittance of debt or punishment. In time it also referred to amnesty or exemption from taxation. In NT usage the verb means “to let go,” “to leave behind,” or “to send away.” Hence, the noun can be (and frequently is) translated “forgiveness” as well as “remission” (",{"href":"?bref=Acts.5.31","r":"Acts.5.31","rawR":"Acts.5.31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.5.31","value":"Acts.5.31"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 5:31"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Acts.13.38","r":"Acts.13.38","rawR":"Acts.13.38","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.13.38","value":"Acts.13.38"}],"t":"ref","v":"13:38"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Acts.26.18","r":"Acts.26.18","rawR":"Acts.26.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.26.18","value":"Acts.26.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"26:18"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Eph.1.7","r":"Eph.1.7","rawR":"Eph.1.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Eph.1.7","value":"Eph.1.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Eph 1:7"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Col.1.14","r":"Col.1.14","rawR":"Col.1.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Col.1.14","value":"Col.1.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Col 1:14"},"). While forgiveness can be exercised at both the human and divine levels, the forgiveness indicated by the word “remission” is almost always that of God (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.26.28","r":"Matt.26.28","rawR":"Matt.26.28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.26.28","value":"Matt.26.28"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 26:28"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Acts.10.43","r":"Acts.10.43","rawR":"Acts.10.43","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.10.43","value":"Acts.10.43"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 10:43"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Forgiveness_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Forgiveness_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Forgiveness_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Forgiveness"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"RemissionofSins","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Rom 3:25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Rom.3.25","rawQueryValue":"Rom.3.25","sourceRefExact":"Rom.3.25"},{"anchorText":"Rom 4:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Rom.4.7","rawQueryValue":"Rom.4.7","sourceRefExact":"Rom.4.7"},{"anchorText":"Rom 4:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Rom.4.8","rawQueryValue":"Rom.4.8","sourceRefExact":"Rom.4.8"},{"anchorText":"Heb 10:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Heb.10.17","rawQueryValue":"Heb.10.17","sourceRefExact":"Heb.10.17"},{"anchorText":"Mt 26:28","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Matt.26.28","rawQueryValue":"Matt.26.28","sourceRefExact":"Matt.26.28"},{"anchorText":"Mk 1:4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Mark.1.4","rawQueryValue":"Mark.1.4","sourceRefExact":"Mark.1.4"},{"anchorText":"Lk 1:77","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Luke.1.77","rawQueryValue":"Luke.1.77","sourceRefExact":"Luke.1.77"},{"anchorText":"3:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Luke.3.3","rawQueryValue":"Luke.3.3","sourceRefExact":"Luke.3.3"},{"anchorText":"24:47","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Luke.24.47","rawQueryValue":"Luke.24.47","sourceRefExact":"Luke.24.47"},{"anchorText"